From f9f83db5e5805e836f90a2a1336ca494946914b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miller Bath <millerzbath@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:52:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: send a file of any size with hc put, and an
 optional drop_dir

hc put now always sends a file in pieces of at most 8 MB: the first call
makes the file, each later one adds to its end (`append`, the name the
first returned). Small files are one piece, so every size goes the same
way and Herdr's drop on a remote terminal works for big files too
(herdrdev/herdr-app#810).

A core from before `append` would make a new file per piece; hc put sees
the second path differ and says to update hc there.

`drop_dir` in config.toml puts every file in one folder that keeps them,
instead of a folder per terminal removed with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
